lecular formula HO_{2}CCH(OH)CH_{2}CO_{2}H. ... In the citric acid cycle, (S)-malate is an intermediate, formed by the addition of an -OH group on the si face of fumarate.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMalate oxidase (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malate_oxidase)\nciteturn34search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; The systematic name of this enzyme class is (S)-malate:oxygen oxidoreductase.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMalate dehydrogenase (oxaloacetate-decarboxylating) (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malate_dehydrogenase_%28oxaloacetate-decarboxylating%29)\nciteturn34search21 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; The systematic name of this enzyme class is (S)-malate:NAD^{+} oxidoreductase (oxaloacetate-decarboxylating). ... *  Biology\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nArginin (https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arginin)\nciteturn34search22 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago;  DrugBank  | DB00125 ... 238 °C\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSinapoylglucose—malate O-sinapoyltransferase (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinapoylglucose%E2%80%94malate_O-sinapoyltransferase)\nciteturn34search23 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; The systematic name of this enzyme class is 1-O-sinapoyl-beta-D-glucose:(S)-malate O-sinapoyltransferase. ... *  Biology\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInsoluble 20X amino acid solution for yeast medium from BMC Microbiology paper (https://www.reddit.com/r/labrats/comments/1rg0bdy/insoluble_20x_amino_acid_solution_for_yeast/)\nciteturn34reddit24 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; I was following a reciepe from a BMC Microbiology paper: \"A buffered media system for yeast batch culture growth\" from Sonja Billabeck at University of Groningen: ... | Compound                           | Amount (g) for making 500 ml 20x amino acids |\n| Adenine Sulfate                    | 0,2                                          |\n| Arginine HCl                       | 0,2                                          | ... | Lysine HCl                         | 0,3                                          |\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCompound: GDP (https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/compounds/35/)\nciteturn34view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://mediadb.systemsbiology.net/defined_media/compounds/35/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 37\nL0: MediaDB\nL1: \nL2: Username:  Password:\nL3: \nL4: Site Navigation:\nL5:   * 【0†Home Page】\nL6:   * 【1†Compounds】\nL7:   * 【2†Media Formulations】\nL8:   * 【3†Organisms】\nL9:   * 【4†Sources】\nL10:   * 【5†Biomass Compositions】\nL11:   * 【6†Downloads】\nL12:   * 【7†Growth Data】\n"
